# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines who is automatically requested for review when a pull
# request touches specific paths. GitHub uses the LAST matching rule, so
# order from most general to most specific.
#
# Syntax:  <pattern>   <@user or @org/team> [<@user>...]
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Global fallback — any file not matched below
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
*                           @your-org/maintainers

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Infrastructure & CI
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/                    @your-org/devops
.github/workflows/          @your-org/devops
.github/SECURITY.md         @your-org/security

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Documentation
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/                       @your-org/docs-team
README.md                   @your-org/maintainers
CHANGELOG.md                @your-org/maintainers

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source code
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
src/                        @your-org/engineering

# ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security-sensitive files
# ────────────────────────────────────────────
.gitleaks.toml              @your-org/security
.pre-commit-config.yaml     @your-org/security @your-org/devops
